    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit requirement in the owner-create endpoint (`POST /api/owners`).\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n2. Emitted an audit line immediately after the owner is persisted in `addOwner`, carrying the owner id, `customerCode` and `registrationDate`:\n   ```java\n   this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n   AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the success path (after all validation/rejection rules and the save), so it reflects the final persisted values \u2014 including the server-generated `customerCode` and the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`. The log statement runs through the SLF4J \u2192 Logback backend the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to, and the observed output confirms the format: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-02`.\n\nTest results: the acceptance suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
